.TITLE "move"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Moves or renames files and directories. It transfers files from one location to another or changes the name of a file or directory.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**move source destination**
Moves a file or directory to a new location.
> __source__ the target to move | __destination__ the new location

**move old_name new_name**
Renames a file or directory.
> __old_name__ the current name | __new_name__ the target name

**move /y source destination**
Suppresses prompting to confirm you want to overwrite an existing destination file.
> __/y__ overwrite flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Renaming a directory with __move__ is an efficient way to update project structures. Unlike __copy__, __move__ deletes the source file after a successful transfer to the destination.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:copy** **windows:dir**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/move__
